fact WorkItem(id: "WI-1025", description: some(value: "A bare Expr::Ref occurrence is the THIRD carrier of a name, but eval::value_functor answers None for it -- so facts_of / stored_facts_of / is_modifiable / sort_query lowering / the reflect bridge all say 'not a sort reference' for a Value::Node that names one, while the Term::Ref and Value::SymbolRef spellings answer the symbol. Split off from WI-1024, which decided the other four carriers and found this one is NOT a line in that match. TWO THINGS MAKE IT ITS OWN TICKET. (1) NO SINGLE HEAD TEST SEPARATES REFERENT FROM ENCODING ON THIS CARRIER: occ_head answers Functor{Some(reflect ctor)} for a Lambda/If/Let/pattern/arrow occurrence -- an ENCODING, exactly like Dictionary, and reading it as a referent turns a loud TypeMismatch into a silently empty facts_of; Expr::Spliced(v) reads THROUGH to v.head(kb), so Node(Spliced(Requirement)) launders the carrier WI-1024 deliberately excluded straight back in; and restricting to ViewHead::Ref answers None for an applied sort occurrence whose TERM twin answers Some, which is the exact cross-carrier disagreement the ticket would exist to fix -- facts_of(kb, List[T = Int64]) (WI-707) is a live consumer of that shape. So the work is to state what makes an occurrence a REFERENT rather than to widen a match arm. (2) IT OBLIGES THE PAIRED SITES. eval/pattern.rs:326-333 (WI-1016) states the rule: a carrier value_functor accepts must be destructurable by match_constructor_pattern, or MatchDispatch's pre-filter promises an arm that then declines. match_constructor_pattern has no Node arm, so a nullary-constructor pattern arm does not match Node(Expr::Ref(nil)) though it matches both other spellings; effects::detect_cycle has the same hole for a Node resource key. MEASURED: the corpus population is ZERO -- instrumented over all four crates, 41631 value_functor calls, carriers Entity/Term/Int only, no Node ever -- so every arm needs a DRIVEN control, a count proves nothing (WI-815). Sites: eval/eval.rs value_functor; eval/pattern.rs match_constructor_pattern; eval/effects.rs detect_cycle."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "user", at: "2026-08-06T06:07:38Z"))
